      "text": "A traditional Veden men's garment: a knee-length skirt, sometimes of silk, usually worn with a plain shirt and a long coat or robe.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "19" }]
    }
  ],
  "description": [
    {
      "text": "Veden fashion now follows Alethkar's, so the ulatu is out of date. Shallan noted her great-grandfathers would have paired theirs with mink pelts.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "19" }]
    },
    {
      "text": "It resembles the Alethi takama but is usually shorter.",
